scott wrote:

> I have 2 blessed bags of holding full of goodies, cleaver, decent
> armor, some powerful wands (no wishing/death afaik)

Don't carry them both. An accident is just waiting to happen if you do.
Put everything you want to carry in the same one, and leave the other one
as a spare in you cache.

> I am decent with bow should I try to pick off the
> blue ones b4 getting closer?  Im not sure if the dragons are gonna
> whoop me if I get close to them.

Dragons aren't really that tough. By the time you meet them, you can
almost always kill them by hand. Just don't fight two of them at the same
time. That shouldn't be a problem if you manage to lure them away from the
castle walls one-by-one, though. They tend to stay near Kroisos' Castle,
since they "smell" the gems inside.

Make an exception for black dragons, though. If you don't have
disintegration resistance yet, be *very* wary of them.

> Is it gonna cost me alot of money to get any protection now that I am
> lvl 13? I have a potion of gain lvl so im wondering if i should wait
> to buy protection before quaffing it.

Buying protection will cost you 400*13 = 5200 zorkmids now. If you become
level 14, it'll cost you 5600 zorkmids per donation.

And it's not often a good idea to quaff a potion of gain level, by the
way. It's considered wise by lots of us here to keep your level down, so
you won't meet the very tough monsters. Becoming level 14 is an exception,
though, since that's the minimum level required to be allowed to the
Quest.

If I were you, I'd postpone quaffing until you're ready for the Quest in
all other aspects.

